From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oscar M <osm1019@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dodge: Enable real-time 1080p/4K 120fps and clamp 8K to 30fps

Ported to the COS17 OplusCamera. Obfuscated names mapped by method body:
module/a X8 -> u9, wj -> Kk; ak/s0 -> gn/o0 (A, v, y unchanged);
ka/a -> td/b.l; ka/i j1 -> td/g.o1, fps register v12 -> v13.

- u9() returns operation mode 1 (constrained high speed) at 120fps.
- gn/o0 records profiles above 60fps at 120fps and clamps 8K to 30fps.
- td/b.l() accepts 120fps next to 60fps for the high frame rate sizes.
- td/g.buildSession() sends video_30fps for video_size_8k.
---

